{
  "title": "Server search lets unaccent expansions act as LIKE wildcards",
  "description": "list_recipes builds each bare-text token's pattern by \
escaping LIKE metacharacters (escape_like_pattern) and *then* passing the \
pattern through f_unaccent. Six codepoints unaccent to LIKE metacharacters \
(fullwidth ％ U+FF05 and small ﹪ U+FE6A to %, fullwidth ＿ U+FF3F to _, and \
U+2216/U+FE68/U+FF3C to \\), so a query containing them gains wildcard or \
escape behavior after escaping: searching 100％ matches any recipe containing \
'100'.\n\
\n\
This is currently deliberate parity behavior: the iOS local search mirrors it \
exactly (RecipeSearchSupport implements LIKE semantics over the normalized \
pattern), and the shared vector case 'fullwidth percent unaccents to a LIKE \
wildcard after escaping' in shared-test-vectors/search-match-filter.json pins \
it on both sides. But it is arguably a server bug — a user typing a fullwidth \
percent almost certainly wants a literal match.\n\
\n\
If it is worth fixing, escape the pattern *after* unaccenting it on the \
server (f_unaccent of the escaped pattern is otherwise unchanged: no other \
unaccent output contains \\, %, or _), simplify the iOS LIKE matcher back to \
plain substring containment, and update the shared vector case in the same \
PR. If not, delete this issue; the behavior is documented and pinned either \
way.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "api",
    "search",
    "ios",
  ],
